hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19251","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us: I was informed from Abu al-Zinad, Muraqqi ibn Sayfi al-Tamimi narrated to me: He testified upon his grandfather Riyah ibn Rabiy al-Hanzali the scribe that he informed him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned like the hadith of Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"19252","Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad who said: al-Muraqqi ibn Sayfi informed me from his grandfather Riyah ibn Rabiy, brother of Hanzalah the scribe, that he informed him that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith."
"19253","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad who said: Muraqqi ibn Sayfi narrated to me, he said: My grandfather Riyah ibn Rabiy, brother of Hanzalah the scribe, narrated to me that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in an expedition with Khalid ibn al-Walid at its vanguard, and he mentioned Riyah and his origin, and he mentioned the hadith."
"19254","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Uthman from Hanzalah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we mentioned Paradise and the Fire until they were as eye-witness. I went to my family and laughed and played with my family and child. I remembered what I was at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I went out and met Abu Bakr. I said: O Abu Bakr, Hanzalah has become a hypocrite. He said: What is that? I said: We were at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we mentioned Paradise and the Fire until they were as eye-witness. I went to my family and laughed and played with my child and family. He said: We do that. I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: O Hanzalah, if you remained in your houses as you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you on your beds and on the roads. O Hanzalah, an hour and an hour."
"19255","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Imran meaning al-Qattan narrated to us from Qatadah from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir from Hanzalah al-Usayyidi who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when we are with you we are so, and when we leave you we are otherwise. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if you remained upon the state you are upon with me, the angels would shake hands with you and shade you with their wings."
